// land-run.bml — a movement's close in one call: write, append, edit, witness,
// observe, commit, rebase and publish. The landing itself is
// form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-landing.bml, so a movement lands inside its own
// call; git is the crossing it needs. Native callers supply a node through
// cell_input and receive the typed publication receipt directly.
// stdin: one JSON line — files, append, edits, witness, paths, subject, body, restart.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-landing.bml
section [form.bml] {
 ld-run();
}
